Block scalar editing
description: the block_scalar_editing state
- >
  The AUTHORED header (`|`, `|-`, `|+`, `>`, ...) is PROJECTED verbatim from the concrete and KEPT
  - commits re-emit the same header over the edited lines (a fresh block typed via `|` is authored
  `|`). The text lines edit below it exactly as they sit in the source, indented, in the ordinary
  editor styling - not a foreign-looking box. BIRTH is the header + ENTER (the whole header can be
  typed first - `|-`, `>-`; a digit indicator refuses, visibly): a valid "" scalar materializes
  per the hole's shape (named / ordinal / the empty container's whole value / the omni self line
  at its row; FLOW refuses - the flow grammar owns Enter) and the textarea opens with the body
  pending in the cursor. A block SELF-VALUE line edits the same way. Enter is a NEWLINE here,
  never a commit; leaving from an edge line (arrows) commits the body
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '`block_scalar_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', '', '`block_scalar_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`ctrl_enter`', '', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`tab`', '', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', '', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`click_outside`', '', '[scalar_committed](*::server:yamlover-editor:scalar_committed)']
  - ['`up_arrow`', 'caret on the first line', '[focus_prev](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`up_arrow`', 'otherwise', '`block_scalar_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`down_arrow`', 'caret on the last line', '[focus_next](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_next)']
  - ['`down_arrow`', 'otherwise', '`block_scalar_editing` (stays)']
